From cdb3f3278567e56944736c1c24d0485d7d719c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:50:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/92] llama, deepseek4, server, logits : V4.1's exact
 encoder-only prefill, on by default (SiegeLadder P4; LLAMA_DSV4_ENC_ONLY=0 -
 off) and the G4 CPU-lane probe (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G4_PROBE, measurement, off)

P4: V4.1 is a causal encoder-decoder - of layers 20-39 only layer 20 (the last KV source) leaves anything for later
positions (its compressed rows, index keys, compressor state); layers 21-39 write only their window rings, so the
decoder's reach is (39 - 20) * (n_swa - 1) = 2413 positions. Inside every llama_decode call a ubatch without outputs whose
positions all lie more than that before the first position the call hands back (an output, or the call's end) runs layers
0-19 and layer 20's cache writes only (build_attention_impl src_only), and the graph ends there. Checked: bitwise at -ub 1
(llama-logits score, 586 encoder-only ubatches) with a tight negative control (reach 2412 differs at the first target);
at -ub 8192 the answer's top-20 logprobs equal a control with the same batching. Consultant 30K 549 -> 845 tok/s,
128K 172 s, 256K 343 s (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.135-4.136). The server cuts the prompt 4 tokens before its end only when
the context runs P4 (llama_dsv4_enc_only); llama-logits takes -b for score mode.

G4 probe: in a decode call without a drive wait the last k(n) experts held in the host tier and off the card stand for a
CPU lane's - dropped (1), dropped + the reply waits k x T us (2), control with weight 0 but loaded (3), or 2 + staged after
the call's loads (4); counters in print_stats.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
